OL,3,GNEWSAPeople just brazenly ask: 'Have
OL,4,Ayou got any cheap tobacco?'
OL,5,
OL,6,FMohammed Rajak has run his family
OL,7,Fgrocery store in Glasgow's East End for
OL,8,F35 years.
OL,10,FHe's seen his business change over that
OL,11,Ftime, but he says the biggest threat to
OL,12,Fhis livelihood right now are shops
OL,13,Fselling illicit tobacco and vapes.
OL,15,FHe says his own shop does not sell such
OL,16,Fproducts but there are stores very
OL,17,Fclose by that do.
OL,19,F"Customers know that," Rajak says.
